# V16's baseline: the considered-and-CLOSED records that must SURVIVE --
# an option REJECTED, or DEFERRED under a stated trigger.
#
# `<id>` then whitespace then the marker, which runs to end of line and may
# contain spaces. `#` comments and blank lines are skipped.
#
# This file exists because V16 is the one rule not derivable from the spec
# text alone. The others ask "is this file well formed"; V16 asks "is this
# record still here", which is a claim about EDITS OVER TIME -- and no single
# text can say what used to be in it. So the checker owns the rule and this
# repo owns the list.
#
# The marker is a substring of the record, not the whole thing. Long enough to
# be specific, short enough that rewording the surrounding prose does not fire
# it: what must survive is the DECISION, not the sentence.
#
# Adding a line here is how a newly closed option becomes load-bearing.
#
# A DEFERRAL needs this more than a rejection does: a rejection reads as a
# closed decision, a deferral reads as an unbuilt feature, and a compaction
# pass drops it thinking "not built = not needed". T10 and T14 are deferrals;
# their rows name the condition that would reopen them.
# Removing one is a reviewed decision -- it says the option is no longer worth
# recording, which is exactly the trade V16 forbids making silently for bytes.

# T6 named what it deliberately did NOT build, each with its reason. Without
# this, a later reader re-proposes the cassette axis or shellcheck and nothing
# says they were already considered and dropped.
T6   DROPPED

# V24 rejected shipping the dev shell a BUILT mth in favour of a cargo-run
# shim: a package must compile before the shell opens, so one error locks you
# out of the shell you need to fix it.
V24  a built package
T20  REJECTED: microlith writing an inline markdownlint directive
T23  REJECTED: auto-writing a single `complete all tasks` milestone
T10  DROPPED: multi-version support & AUTODETECTION
# T29 rejected `derive --format json` on a fact about a PUBLISHED artifact:
# an old `mth` ignores the flag and exits 0 with prose. Without this line the
# rejection reads as an unbuilt alternative somebody should get round to.
T29  REJECTED: `derive --format json`
T14  DROPPED: a parallel `nk:` skill set

# V31 defers a checker for condition 4; the denylist cannot live in the repo
# it guards. Without this line a later pass reads it as an unbuilt feature.
V31  A checker is DEFERRED

# T26d absorbed the MECHANICAL half of cavekit-extensions' supersession and
# refused the other half outright. Without this line the LLM proposer reads as
# an unbuilt feature somebody should get round to, rather than as a decision --
# and the seam it keeps is V6, which is the whole reason this crate is CPU-only.
T26d ⊥ ABSORBED & ⊥ EVER: mode B
V44  REJECTED: actionlint ALONE

# V46 rejected FANNING OUT over several paths, choosing a usage error. Without
# this line the fan-out reads as an unbuilt convenience rather than a decision
# with a trigger.
V46  REJECTED: FAN OUT

# V47 rejected keying V11 on the heading instead of on the rows, because
# FORMAT.md permits ordinary `##` headings that open no section at all.
# Without this line it reads as the obvious fix nobody got round to.
V47  REJECTED: keying V11 on the HEADING

# V48 rejected lifting the done rows OUT, and the milestone-at-a-time variant
# that was supposed to rescue it. Both are the obvious compaction, so without
# this line the stub reads as an odd choice somebody should simplify.
V48  Lifting a done row OUT

# V49 rejected giving `tasks` a distinct exit code for "read nothing, but the
# file is not empty of candidates". Without this line it reads as the obvious
# signal nobody got round to adding.
V49  REJECTED: a distinct EXIT CODE
